  "caption": "Deadline week: Quinn sat locked in one position for eight hours a day. By Friday, the spot between the shoulder blades was burning, right where you can't reach.\n\nMid-back stiffness often builds when we hold the upper back bent for hours with little rotation or extension. It's less about 'bad' posture and more about posture that never changes.\n\nWhat often helps: seated rotations, chair-back extensions and overhead reaches a few times a day, strength work like rows, band pull-aparts and arm raises, slow full breaths, and changing positions often. A gentle foam roller can feel nice too.\n\nConstant or severe pain, night waking, a fall, band-like chest pain, breathlessness, fever or unexplained weight change needs prompt medical attention.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
